Q: How do I update array of objects in Zustand? A: <p>The setter function should return the new state, not imperatively update it.</p>
<p>Try:</p>
<pre class="lang-javascript prettyprint-override"><code>o =&gt; {
    set((state) =&gt; ({ MasterSteps:  [...state.MasterSteps, o ] }))
}
</code></pre>
<p>Try:</p>
<pre class="lang-javascript prettyprint-override"><code>const useStore = create((set) =&gt; ({
    ...initialState,
    routeKey: &quot;&quot;,
    MasterSteps: [],
    setRoute: (routeKeyToUse) =&gt; {
        set((state) =&gt; ({
            routeKey: routeKeyToUse;
        }))
    },
    setMasterSteps: (o) =&gt; {
        set((state) =&gt; ({
            MasterSteps: [...state.MasterSteps, o ]
        }))},
}));
</code></pre>
<p>Also what is the definition of initialData? If it provides a value for MasterSteps, it's overwritten by the later MasterSteps = [].</p>
